    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="letterhead">THE ROCKEFELLER FOUNDATION <lb/>49 WEST
                        49th STREET,<rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">NEW YORK</rs> 20
                        <lb/><!-- kleiner und auf der linken Blattseite: -->THE HUMANITIES <lb/><rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__3324" type="person">DAVID H. STEVENS</rs>,
                        DIRECTOR <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3406" type="person">John
                            Marshall</rs>, ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR <lb/></fw><dateline><date
                            when="1946-04-01">April 1, 1946</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                        Tillich</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>Thank you for <rs ref="#L10923" type="letter">your letter of March 28</rs>, about
                    <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1262" type="person">Professor Marck</rs>&apos;s book
                    and his need of help in getting parts of it translated to make it suitable for
                    publication in this country.</p>
                <p>You will understand this whole matter was left pending when <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__3324" type="person">Stevens</rs> went to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__710" type="place">Japan</rs>, with a memorandum by
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3324" type="person">Stevens</rs> in late
                    January to the effect that you would let us have some recommendation after you
                    had seen <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1262" type="person">Professor Marck</rs>
                    in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__105" type="place">Chicago</rs>. Thus, with <rs
                        ref="#L10923" type="letter">your letter of March 28</rs>, I think I have the
                    basis I need for seeing what can be arranged and would be glad to explore that
                    possibility as promptly as I can.</p>
                <closer><salute>Yours sincerely,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3406"
                            type="person">John Marshall</rs>.</signed>
                    <fw place="bottom" type="adressline"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Professor Paul Tillich</rs>
                        <lb/>Union Theological Seminary <lb/>Broadway at 120th Street <lb/><rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs>, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__865" type="place">New York</rs>
                        <lb/>
                        <lb/>JM: EHD</fw>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
